# What EAS Build does NOT upload. Repo root, deliberately.
#
# Why this file exists at all: native/assets/data.json is generated by
# tools/build_site.py and gitignored (rule 20.3 — generated artifacts are never
# tracked), but native/src/data.js imports it directly, so Metro needs it. EAS's
# default git client uploads `git archive`, which cannot see an untracked file, and
# the build dies with "Unable to resolve module ../assets/data.json" in the Bundle
# JavaScript phase. That is builds 46c3d5df and 395d5a93.
#
# The fix is EAS_NO_VCS=1, which switches eas-cli to copying the working tree and
# honouring this file. Two consequences worth knowing:
#
#   1. It must live at the REPO ROOT, not in native/. The no-VCS client resolves its
#      root with `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`, so a .easignore inside native/ is
#      never read. (native/metro.config.js also needs ../core, so the upload has to
#      start above native/ regardless.)
#   2. When .easignore exists, .gitignore is NOT consulted — for anything. Every
#      exclusion has to be repeated here, including the secrets ones. Adding a new
#      gitignore rule for something sensitive means adding it here too.

.git
node_modules

# Secrets. .gitignore's copies of these rules do not apply once this file exists.
.env
.env.*
*.token
.netlify/
backend/.dev.vars

# The feedback Worker is its own deployable; the app only knows its URL.
backend/

# Generated output and source data: several hundred megabytes, none of which the
# native bundle touches. native/assets/data.json is NOT under data/ and stays.
site/
data/
tools/

# Regenerated by EAS from app.json; never upload a local prebuild.
native/android/
native/ios/
native/.expo/
native/coverage/

# Local build output. `native/build-out/` holds the APKs built here and handed
# to his phone — **101.8 MB of the 167 MB archive** when this was measured on
# 2026-09-17, which is to say most of it, and an EAS build has no use for an
# APK a previous build made. Gitignored, but .easignore does not consult
# .gitignore (see the note at the top), so it has to be named again here.
native/build-out/
.expo-export/

# Prose and the content review. Neither is read by the bundler.
docs/
review/

# Not part of the app.
native/__tests__/
native/jest.setup.js
native/flows/
native/screenshots/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
.DS_Store
